<!--
  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.TypeSystemOverview
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:btype="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <idea>Overview of ValueType kinds, generics, and type expressions.</idea>

  <documentation>
    BlockML knows four ValueType kinds at language level — each names a semantic meaning:

    PrimitiveType — atomic scalar semantics; no stored values on the type itself.
    Examples: Boolean, Integer, Decimal, Float, Text, URL, Version, FullyQualifiedName.

    StructType — custom value objects; structure via properties.
    Examples: Size3D, Color, Address, Transform. Parameterized types (Box(T)) are StructTypes
    with genericTypes — not a separate branch.

    EnumType — specialized StructType with finite allowed values via _values aggregation.
    Examples: Direction, Face, StudType.

    ConstantType — singleton value domain; one configured literal.
    Example: Constant(Text){value="auto"} for union alternatives.

    Type expressions combine named types — they are not new BlockML type classes:
    • Multiplicity: Integer[], Integer[3], Text[0..n]
    • Unions: Boolean | Integer, Constant(Text){value="auto"} | Float
    • Generic application: Box(Integer) — round parentheses in type attributes
    • Instance configuration: Text{maxLength=100}, Decimal{precision=10, scale=2}
    • bml:Self — resolves to effective current Block type after inheritance
    • T — generic parameter reference from declaring Block's genericTypes

    Only ValueTypes may appear where a bare type name is required (Property type,
    Capability inputType/outputType). Any Block FQN is valid in aggregation and association
    type attributes. ValueTypes never store data — Properties own all concrete values.
  </documentation>

  <references>
